# A proposed rules.d/ fragment, for the `check` golden and the corpus sweep. The name
# sorts before every shipped file, so the rule is merged ahead of the whole host ruleset
# and is reached before any rule that denied.
#
# It allows the denied execute of the copied grep, which is #120's `exec-before-N` row:
# measured `allow (rule=1)` on Rocky 8, 9 and 10. Every other denial in the fixture stays
# denied, and the loader's own records come back unknown because §6's stale `exe=` rewrite
# fires on them (#120 K3).
allow perm=execute all : path=/tmp/live/probe-grep
